    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The present building replaced Agrippa's temple after fires in 80 and 110, yet carries Agrippa's inscription, so its date and even its original purpose remain uncertain.</li><li>Its consecration as a church in 609 saved it from the abandonment and worst spoliation that befell most of ancient <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>'s buildings.</li><li>As the best-preserved Roman monumental building, it has been a model for domes and porticoes from Brunelleschi's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florence">Florence</a> to Jefferson's University of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The oculus has never been covered, so rain falls on the floor, which slopes about 30 centimetres to its drains; at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pentecost">Pentecost</a> firefighters throw red rose petals through it from the roof.</p></aside>
    </section>

